            <div xml:id="d612">

                <pb facs="0703" n="637" sameAs="frus:frus1934v05/pg637"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">819.74/290: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Panama</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gonzalez</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Panama</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-07-06T13:00:00-05:00">July 6, 1934—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:14 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>124. Referring to my despatch No. 213 of May 2d, may I express the sincere hope
                    that telegraphic instructions be given me immediately to propose to Panamanian
                    Government the transfer of Puerto Obaldía and La Palma radio stations in
                    accordance with draft agreement transmitted <pb facs="0704" n="638"
                        xml:id="pg638"/> with that despatch. I consider it highly appropriate to be
                    able to announce an agreement on this matter before the arrival of President
                    Roosevelt.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gonzalez</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
